  {
   "text": "The rocket is built in the project as \"Toy rocket\" (design d1): a 40 mm body tube lifted 8 mm off the bed, a 40 mm pointed cone nose, and three 4 mm fins at 120 degrees that touch the bed and carry the body. The total height is 150 mm, as you asked, and it fits the A1 mini. Body diameter, nose height, lift, fin height, fin span and fin thickness were my guesses, shown on the sheet and confirmed as they were.\n\nThe plan check did not fully pass, and I have not changed the part to force it:\n- **Overall size:** the plan said 80 x 80 x 150 mm, which was my estimate. The part measures 61.7 x 71.3 x 150 mm, which follows from the confirmed fin span.\n- **Feature count:** 5 against 4 planned, because the fin join added one step.\n- **Minimum wall:** 0 mm, caused by the sharp nose tip. A cone tip is zero-thickness by nature.\n\nThe rocket is watertight and matches the confirmed sizes. To clear the wall check, I can cut a small flat on the nose tip (for example 2 mm across), which makes it slightly blunt. Otherwise, the rocket is ready as it stands. Tell me which you want, and whether you want to refine any size in Model before slicing for the A1 mini."
  }
